@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor, without a leading dot on root property names ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16); [validated by: names a missing root property without a leading dot](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L184)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- A failing field path uses the declared property name even when that name contains a slash or is numeric, renders array indexes in brackets, and does not include the supplied value ([validated by: names a slash-bearing property without exposing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L8); [validated by: names an array element field with its index and expected type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L51); [validated by: distinguishes a numeric object property from an array index](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.numeric-property.test.ts#L7); [validated by: names a nested numeric object property without array brackets](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.numeric-property.test.ts#L24)).
+- When a schema explicitly sets `additionalProperties: false`, a rejected extra property is named along with the `additionalProperties` constraint, without exposing its value ([validated by: names an explicitly forbidden extra property without exposing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L29)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults.
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- Registering a static tool with an invalid schema throws an error naming that tool, even if another static tool previously registered the same schema object before it changed ([validated by: rejects an invalid static input schema when registering its named tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L95); [validated by: rejects a changed invalid schema when registering a second static tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.static-reregistration.test.ts#L5)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: keeps the schema compiled at registration when a static definition changes](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L75)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: uses each current schema and compiles each schema object once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L131)).
+- Distinct dynamic schema objects enforce their own rules even when they reuse the same JSON Schema `$id` ([validated by: uses the current dynamic schema when distinct schemas reuse an id](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L113)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
+- The orchestrator executes at most `maxToolRounds` tool-call rounds, including rejected calls; a tool call requested in the final provider round is not executed ([validated by: executes no more than maxToolRounds rejected tool calls](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L438)).
